  "answer": "In Q1 2026, Customer Success noted a sharp increase in citation-error tickets; an audit of 210 accuracy-related tickets found: Incorrect File Links (42%), Missing Page Numbers (28%), Empty Citations (18%), and Broken Links (12%) [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. In Q2, citation-accuracy tickets declined steadily after the April product release: January 72, February 79, March 88, April 42, May 31, and June 24 [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The April citation validation engine and PDF parser updates resolved most incorrect/missing citation complaints [NL-011#NL-011-S03]. However, remaining May and June citation tickets were almost entirely linked to scanned, image-only PDFs, where TutorChat cannot establish page-level citation anchors [NL-011#NL-011-S05], and the current indexing pipeline lacks advanced OCR processing [NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nThe planned work that directly addresses this scanned-document problem is the **Advanced OCR Pipeline**, scheduled for release in August 2026: it will integrate an OCR engine into the KnowledgeHub ingestion queue [NL-010#NL-010-S10] and automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned files, enabling page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
